00:02:04.791 --> 00:02:06.292
It's a lot of books.

00:02:06.292 --> 00:02:08.361
As a guy who just finished
my second, I admire someone

00:02:08.361 --> 00:02:10.497
that has written
this many books.

00:02:10.497 --> 00:02:12.265
But let's just start
sorta just generally

00:02:12.265 --> 00:02:13.500
with what's going
on in the world,

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:14.734
which will kind of
get us to the book,

00:02:14.734 --> 00:02:16.803
because that's really
what this is all about.

00:02:16.803 --> 00:02:19.105
COVID's a little
bananas right now,

00:02:19.105 --> 00:02:22.509 align:start size:81% position:19%
or at least the
reaction to COVID.

00:02:22.509 --> 00:02:24.744
Where are you at at this
point with the whole thing?

00:02:24.744 --> 00:02:28.148 line:0%
- So the pandemic is over
as far as I'm concerned

00:02:28.148 --> 00:02:29.682 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
from a public
policy perspective.

00:02:29.682 --> 00:02:31.584 line:0%
That does not mean that the
pandemic is like technically

00:02:31.584 --> 00:02:34.087 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
over, like, you can walk
outside without vaccination,

00:02:34.087 --> 00:02:35.622 align:start size:81% position:19%
without masks,
everything's fine.

00:02:35.622 --> 00:02:38.224
But what it does mean is that
all public policy is designed

00:02:38.224 --> 00:02:39.626
to do is achieve
certain objectives.

00:02:39.626 --> 00:02:41.728
Originally we were told
that the public policy

00:02:41.728 --> 00:02:43.830
with regard to COVID
was designed to prevent

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:45.498
the overrunning
of the hospitals.

00:02:45.498 --> 00:02:47.500 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so we all locked
down and we all masked up

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:49.469 align:start size:97% position:3%
and then we prevented the
overrunning of the hospitals.

00:02:49.469 --> 00:02:51.604
And then the idea was okay,
well now we're gonna delay

00:02:51.604 --> 00:02:53.873
indefinitely until we
can get to the vaccine.

00:02:53.873 --> 00:02:56.109 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then these miraculous
vaccines came around

00:02:56.109 --> 00:02:58.044
and the idea was okay, the
vaccines are now available.

00:02:58.044 --> 00:03:00.547 align:start size:97% position:3%
And then we said, okay,
well we'll until every adult

00:03:00.547 --> 00:03:02.348 align:start size:97% position:3%
has had the chance to either
take it or not take it

00:03:02.348 --> 00:03:04.651 align:start position:0%
as the case may be because
they are super duper effective.

00:03:04.651 --> 00:03:06.085
And now we've reached that.

00:03:06.085 --> 00:03:08.188 align:start size:97% position:3%
And now the problem is
there's no actual next goal.

00:03:08.188 --> 00:03:10.423
And this is something that
is driving me up a wall.

00:03:10.423 --> 00:03:13.059 align:start size:84% position:16%
If you listen to
people on CNN or MSNBC

00:03:13.059 --> 00:03:15.428 align:start size:97% position:3%
or on the administration
talk, it seems that the goal

00:03:15.428 --> 00:03:16.629
is zero COVID.

00:03:16.629 --> 00:03:18.631 align:start size:88% position:13%
Like every single person
in the United States

00:03:18.631 --> 00:03:20.900 align:start size:97% position:3%
getting the vaccine and
then COVID just going away.

00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:23.803
And no one actually thinks
this is ever going to happen.

00:03:23.803 --> 00:03:26.606 align:start size:97% position:3%
This is a disease that has
been seeded over every country

00:03:26.606 --> 00:03:27.874
pretty much on planet earth.

00:03:27.874 --> 00:03:29.809
It's taken a minimum
of four million lives,

00:03:29.809 --> 00:03:31.311
probably closer to six million

00:03:31.311 --> 00:03:33.012 align:start size:88% position:13%
if you look at the
actual stats from India.

00:03:33.012 --> 00:03:34.814 align:start size:94% position:6%
And certainly if you
include the actual number

00:03:34.814 --> 00:03:37.183 align:start size:94% position:6%
of dead from China, a
lot more lives than that.

00:03:37.183 --> 00:03:40.286
And the notion that this
is just going to go away

00:03:40.286 --> 00:03:42.488 align:start size:94% position:6%
if we yell at people to
get the vaccine, is crazy.

00:03:42.488 --> 00:03:44.757 align:start size:97% position:3%
Which means to me that
basically now that every adult

00:03:44.757 --> 00:03:46.960 align:start size:88% position:13%
has had the opportunity
to take the vaccine

00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:49.929
and because, thank God, this
disease is not really affecting

00:03:49.929 --> 00:03:52.198
kids in severe ways,
like the total number

00:03:52.198 --> 00:03:53.633
of kids under the age
of 18 who have died

00:03:53.633 --> 00:03:57.737 align:start size:97% position:3%
is still under 350 in a
sub-population of 75 million,

00:03:57.737 --> 00:03:59.272
we're done.

00:03:59.272 --> 00:04:01.207
I mean, as far as public, what
public policy can accomplish

00:04:01.207 --> 00:04:03.576 align:start size:97% position:3%
or should seek to accomplish,
we are pretty much done

00:04:03.576 --> 00:04:05.111
at this point.

00:04:05.111 --> 00:04:07.380
And the problem for the left
is that they set, as a goal,

00:04:07.380 --> 00:04:09.716 align:start size:84% position:16%
the idea of zero
COVID back last year

00:04:09.716 --> 00:04:11.150
and now they can't let go of it.

00:04:11.150 --> 00:04:12.685 align:start position:0%
So Biden is kind of stuck
between a rock and a hard place.

00:04:12.685 --> 00:04:14.454 align:start size:94% position:6%
On the one hand, he wants
to declare COVID over

00:04:14.454 --> 00:04:16.589
so we can all go back to work
and everybody can enjoy life

00:04:16.589 --> 00:04:18.124
and he can say that
he beat the thing.

00:04:18.124 --> 00:04:20.326 align:start size:88% position:13%
On the other hand,
he's actually, in order

00:04:20.326 --> 00:04:22.495 align:start position:0%
to do that he has to
acknowledge that we have to live

00:04:22.495 --> 00:04:24.697 align:start size:94% position:6%
with the virus which would
open the can of worms

00:04:24.697 --> 00:04:26.899 align:start size:97% position:3%
that last year Democrats
said we should certainly not

00:04:26.899 --> 00:04:28.368 align:start size:94% position:6%
live with the virus and
anybody who said we should

00:04:28.368 --> 00:04:30.503 align:start size:97% position:3%
live with the virus, like
governor DeSantis in Florida,

00:04:30.503 --> 00:04:32.005
was bad and evil.

00:04:32.005 --> 00:04:33.673 align:start size:94% position:6%
So instead we're gonna get
this ridiculous specter

00:04:33.673 --> 00:04:36.175 align:start size:94% position:6%
of people trying to
scare you into being okay

00:04:36.175 --> 00:04:38.011
with giving up liberties
that really, at this point,

00:04:38.011 --> 00:04:39.779 align:start size:84% position:16%
there's no scientific
rationale for.

00:04:39.779 --> 00:04:41.848 align:start size:97% position:3%
So you're gonna continue
masking your kid even though,

00:04:41.848 --> 00:04:44.517 align:start position:0%
again, this thing is not
radically damaging to children.

00:04:44.517 --> 00:04:47.420 align:start size:97% position:3%
I mean, 810 kids died of
pneumonia in the same period

00:04:47.420 --> 00:04:49.956 align:start size:88% position:13%
that COVID killed
something like 350 kids

00:04:49.956 --> 00:04:52.425 align:start size:97% position:3%
over the course of the
last year and a half or so.

00:04:52.425 --> 00:04:54.027
You're supposed to mask
up your kid to protect

00:04:54.027 --> 00:04:56.062
a 40 year old who decided
not to get the vaccine.

00:04:56.062 --> 00:04:57.697 align:start size:94% position:6%
Or if you're vaccinated
you're supposed to mask up

00:04:57.697 --> 00:05:00.133
in case, God forbid, you give
it to somebody who, again,

00:05:00.133 --> 00:05:01.401
decided not to get the vaccine.

00:05:01.401 --> 00:05:03.369
Like none of that is
good public policy.

00:05:03.369 --> 00:05:05.071
So I'm annoyed by it.

00:05:05.071 --> 00:05:06.272
I'm frustrated by it.

00:05:06.272 --> 00:05:07.807 align:start size:88% position:13%
I also think it's a
bad incentive structure

00:05:07.807 --> 00:05:11.577
because I don't know why I,
who according to the powers

00:05:11.577 --> 00:05:13.012 align:start size:88% position:13%
that be did the right
thing, I got vaccinated.

00:05:13.012 --> 00:05:13.946
My wife got vaccinated.

00:05:13.946 --> 00:05:15.315
My parents got vaccinated.

00:05:15.315 --> 00:05:17.950 align:start size:97% position:3%
Why am I supposed to
penalize myself by masking up

00:05:17.950 --> 00:05:21.421 align:start position:0%
to protect people who are
overtly not only not vaccinating

00:05:21.421 --> 00:05:23.122 align:start size:94% position:6%
but also saying they
don't care whether I wear

00:05:23.122 --> 00:05:23.956
a mask or not.

00:05:23.956 --> 00:05:25.425
It's bizarre.

00:05:25.425 --> 00:05:26.993 align:start size:97% position:3%
- What would you say to
those people at this point?

00:05:26.993 --> 00:05:28.761
Because there obviously
are a lot of people.

00:05:28.761 --> 00:05:31.497
I think it might be as many
as something like 30 to 40%

00:05:31.497 --> 00:05:33.666 align:start size:88% position:13%
of American adults
that are not vaccinated

00:05:33.666 --> 00:05:36.269
that are saying I either had
it and I have the antibodies

00:05:36.269 --> 00:05:38.705 align:start size:81% position:19%
or I just don't
want this vaccine,

00:05:38.705 --> 00:05:40.573 align:start size:94% position:6%
which basically was
produced in about a year.

00:05:40.573 --> 00:05:42.108
Or whatever reasons
that might have.

00:05:42.108 --> 00:05:44.677 align:start size:97% position:3%
What would you say to
those people at this point?

00:05:44.677 --> 00:05:46.279
- So number one, you're a free
and independent human being,

00:05:46.279 --> 00:05:47.714
you're an adult, and
it's your decision.

00:05:47.714 --> 00:05:49.248
That's that's number one.

00:05:49.248 --> 00:05:51.117
Number two, if we're talking
about you already had COVID,

00:05:51.117 --> 00:05:53.086
I certainly see the rationale,
there's some pretty good data

00:05:53.086 --> 00:05:55.321
suggesting that natural
immunity is as strong,

00:05:55.321 --> 00:05:57.724 align:start size:84% position:16%
if not stronger than
vaccine immunity.

00:05:57.724 --> 00:05:59.525 align:start size:88% position:13%
What I would say is
that for a lot of people

00:05:59.525 --> 00:06:01.427 align:start size:94% position:6%
the given evidence shows,
depending on your age

00:06:01.427 --> 00:06:02.662 align:start size:84% position:16%
and depending on
your health factors,

00:06:02.662 --> 00:06:05.365
that your rate of death
from COVID outweighs

00:06:05.365 --> 00:06:07.467 align:start size:88% position:13%
the rate of adverse
effects from the vaccine

00:06:07.467 --> 00:06:09.135 align:start size:84% position:16%
so far as the data
that we have yet seen.

00:06:09.135 --> 00:06:11.337
And this is pretty much
true for everybody above

00:06:11.337 --> 00:06:12.839
the age of 18.

00:06:12.839 --> 00:06:15.375 align:start size:94% position:6%
I haven't seen the data
between 12 and 18 so much,

00:06:15.375 --> 00:06:16.876
and certainly for kids.

00:06:16.876 --> 00:06:19.145
I have very little interest
in vaccinating my seven, five

00:06:19.145 --> 00:06:20.680
and one-year-old at this point.

00:06:20.680 --> 00:06:23.182 align:start size:84% position:16%
But if you're 35 years
old or 40 years old

00:06:23.182 --> 00:06:25.585
and you're saying, "Well, you
know, I thought I got COVID."

00:06:25.585 --> 00:06:26.419
I'm hearing a lot of this.

00:06:26.419 --> 00:06:27.620
"I thought I got COVID,

00:06:27.620 --> 00:06:28.855 align:start size:84% position:16%
but I wasn't actually
tested for COVID.

00:06:28.855 --> 00:06:30.323
I'm sure I had it before."

00:06:30.323 --> 00:06:32.325 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well unless you were
tested for it, it might've

00:06:32.325 --> 00:06:33.159
been something else.

00:06:33.159 --> 00:06:34.427
Right?

00:06:34.427 --> 00:06:35.928
There are a lot of other
sicknesses going around.

00:06:35.928 --> 00:06:36.596
I was sick several times
during the COVID pandemic,

00:06:36.596 --> 00:06:37.430
never got COVID.

00:06:37.430 --> 00:06:39.165
So don't rely on that.

00:06:39.165 --> 00:06:40.600 align:start size:84% position:16%
Take into account
your own risk factors

00:06:40.600 --> 00:06:42.802 align:start size:97% position:3%
and then seriously consider
getting the vaccine.

00:06:42.802 --> 00:06:45.004
Because, frankly, the
risks from the vaccine,

00:06:45.004 --> 00:06:48.841 align:start position:0%
from what I'm seeing in the
data, are not particularly high.

00:06:48.841 --> 00:06:51.444
And the risks from COVID
are, depending on your age

00:06:51.444 --> 00:06:54.414 align:start size:97% position:3%
maybe somewhat higher, maybe
a multiple times higher.

00:06:54.414 --> 00:06:57.016 align:start position:0%
But again, I respect your
abilities and individual choose

00:06:57.016 --> 00:06:58.551
as long as you're willing to
live with the consequences.

00:06:58.551 --> 00:07:00.319 align:start size:97% position:3%
If you don't get the vaccine
and then you get sick,

00:07:00.319 --> 00:07:01.888 align:start size:84% position:16%
you know, that would
be a you problem,

00:07:01.888 --> 00:07:04.257
don't don't come to public
policy seeking a solution.

00:07:04.257 --> 00:07:05.491
- Right.

00:07:05.491 --> 00:07:06.993 align:start size:88% position:13%
To that point though how
have in the last year

00:07:06.993 --> 00:07:09.162 align:start size:84% position:16%
have you figured out
who you can trust

00:07:09.162 --> 00:07:11.397 align:start size:84% position:16%
or what institutions
you can trust?

00:07:11.397 --> 00:07:14.500
Because it seems to me we've
just seen a complete collapse

00:07:14.500 --> 00:07:18.604 align:start size:97% position:3%
across the board, political,
cultural, you know,

00:07:18.604 --> 00:07:20.473
journalistic, just
the entire thing

00:07:20.473 --> 00:07:22.008
has completely collapsed.

00:07:22.008 --> 00:07:23.643
And that's what people ask me
almost more than anything else

00:07:23.643 --> 00:07:25.144 align:start size:84% position:16%
at this point, "Dave,
who do you trust?

00:07:25.144 --> 00:07:26.813 align:start size:97% position:3%
How do you figure out how
to make some sense of this?"

00:07:26.813 --> 00:07:28.881
- I mean the way that I
determine who to trust

00:07:28.881 --> 00:07:31.851 align:start position:0%
is whether people were skeptical
of the official narrative

00:07:31.851 --> 00:07:33.719
but were basing that in data.

00:07:33.719 --> 00:07:36.088 align:start size:97% position:3%
So, for example, one of the
people who I personally trust,

00:07:36.088 --> 00:07:38.191
a guy named Dr. Marty Makary
from Johns Hopkins' University.

00:07:38.191 --> 00:07:40.626 align:start size:97% position:3%
Very early on, he and I
talked pretty much every week

00:07:40.626 --> 00:07:42.128
on the show.

00:07:42.128 --> 00:07:44.797 align:start size:97% position:3%
And very early on, he was very
skeptical of the lockdowns.

00:07:44.797 --> 00:07:46.499 align:start size:84% position:16%
He was very
skeptical of the idea

00:07:46.499 --> 00:07:48.134
that if you're 20 years old
you shouldn't be working

00:07:48.134 --> 00:07:51.170
or that we should be not
treating people who are 20

00:07:51.170 --> 00:07:52.605
in a different way than
we were treating people

00:07:52.605 --> 00:07:54.207
who are 70, for example.

00:07:54.207 --> 00:07:55.741
Because he was skeptical
of that but he was taking

00:07:55.741 --> 00:07:57.310
the science pretty seriously

00:07:57.310 --> 00:07:59.111
I had a lot of respect for that.

00:07:59.111 --> 00:08:00.980 align:start size:97% position:3%
Same thing with Jay
Bhattacharya from Stanford.

00:08:00.980 --> 00:08:03.282
If you just bought hook, line
and sinker the actual official

00:08:03.282 --> 00:08:05.251 align:start size:84% position:16%
narrative throughout
and the idea,

00:08:05.251 --> 00:08:06.719
and you never cited the data.

00:08:06.719 --> 00:08:09.755
If you ever at any point
said, "The science says..."

00:08:09.755 --> 00:08:11.524 align:start size:88% position:13%
Then I have pretty
much a problem with you

00:08:11.524 --> 00:08:13.860 align:start size:97% position:3%
because science is a process,
science is not a person

00:08:13.860 --> 00:08:15.328
or an institution.

00:08:15.328 --> 00:08:17.096
And so there's sort of a
group of people who I think

00:08:17.096 --> 00:08:19.098 align:start size:84% position:16%
were skeptical of
some of the narratives

00:08:19.098 --> 00:08:21.701
and who would do a good job.

00:08:21.701 --> 00:08:23.870 align:start size:94% position:6%
It similar you decide
who to trust in politics.

00:08:23.870 --> 00:08:26.072 align:start position:0%
They do a good job sort of
steel manning the other argument

00:08:26.072 --> 00:08:27.240 align:start size:88% position:13%
and then say, "Okay,
and here's where I think

00:08:27.240 --> 00:08:28.674
the flaws are."

00:08:28.674 --> 00:08:30.176 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they'd give a nuanced
picture of the data

00:08:30.176 --> 00:08:31.444
as opposed to people who are
just like, "You listen to me,

00:08:31.444 --> 00:08:32.979
and if you don't listen
to me, you're an idiot."

00:08:32.979 --> 00:08:34.514
In which case I think pretty
much always you don't listen

00:08:34.514 --> 00:08:36.048
to those people.

00:08:36.048 --> 00:08:38.084
- Right, so this will kind
of segue us to the book,

00:08:38.084 --> 00:08:40.086 align:start size:84% position:16%
but are you surprised
in the last year,

00:08:40.086 --> 00:08:42.522
I remember like two or
three weeks into COVID,

00:08:42.522 --> 00:08:44.357
it was one of the many
times in the past year

00:08:44.357 --> 00:08:46.592
that Ben Shapiro has
trended on Twitter

00:08:46.592 --> 00:08:48.928
because you said the
very obvious statement,

00:08:48.928 --> 00:08:51.197 align:start size:84% position:16%
in essence that we
are gonna have to live

00:08:51.197 --> 00:08:52.999
with a certain amount of death.

00:08:52.999 --> 00:08:55.501 align:start size:88% position:13%
A certain amount is,
it's just what actuaries

00:08:55.501 --> 00:08:58.004
have to deal with when they're
figuring out insurance rates.

00:08:58.004 --> 00:08:59.906
And that's just the
reality of life.

00:08:59.906 --> 00:09:01.173 align:start size:84% position:16%
And of course everyone
in Media Matters

00:09:01.173 --> 00:09:03.075
and all the usual
clowns were saying

00:09:03.075 --> 00:09:04.644 align:start size:84% position:16%
that Ben Shapiro wants
to kill old people

00:09:04.644 --> 00:09:06.112
and everything else.

00:09:06.112 --> 00:09:08.314 align:start size:97% position:3%
But are you, related to that,
are you sort of surprised

00:09:08.314 --> 00:09:10.082
how quickly everyone folded?

00:09:10.082 --> 00:09:13.152
And even now you can sense
that there's a certain amount

00:09:13.152 --> 00:09:16.055 align:start size:94% position:6%
of people in the media
that want lockdowns again,

00:09:16.055 --> 00:09:17.723 align:start size:84% position:16%
they want more
government programs.

00:09:17.723 --> 00:09:19.725
Like they just, they're
getting off on this.

00:09:19.725 --> 00:09:21.294
They just, they just like it.

00:09:21.294 --> 00:09:22.528
- Yeah.

00:09:22.528 --> 00:09:23.996
I mean, I think that
that is very true.

00:09:23.996 --> 00:09:25.932
I think that this has become
almost a pagan worship ceremony

00:09:25.932 --> 00:09:27.166
for a lot of people.

00:09:27.166 --> 00:09:29.068
Because again, I'm
not anti-masking

00:09:29.068 --> 00:09:30.303
under certain circumstances.

00:09:30.303 --> 00:09:32.305 align:start size:88% position:13%
I'm not anti-masking
for un-vaccinated people

00:09:32.305 --> 00:09:33.673
who are with other
un-vaccinated people

00:09:33.673 --> 00:09:35.107
who are vulnerable to COVID.

00:09:35.107 --> 00:09:37.677 align:start size:97% position:3%
I mean, I was never
anti-Fauci until he started

00:09:37.677 --> 00:09:40.346
pretty much overtly lying to
us in a wide variety of cases.

00:09:40.346 --> 00:09:42.315 align:start position:0%
I've been pro-vaccine
throughout this entire pandemic.

00:09:42.315 --> 00:09:45.685 align:start size:97% position:3%
So yeah, I find it
shocking however the number

00:09:45.685 --> 00:09:48.054
of people who are much more
interested in castigating

00:09:48.054 --> 00:09:50.590 align:start size:97% position:3%
people who are using their own
independent risk assessment

00:09:50.590 --> 00:09:53.192 align:start size:84% position:16%
and coming to a
different conclusion,
or analyzing the data

00:09:53.192 --> 00:09:54.994
in a different way but
looking at the data.

00:09:54.994 --> 00:09:57.797
I'm shocked at the number
of people who have decided

00:09:57.797 --> 00:09:59.432 align:start size:97% position:3%
that they are more interested
in the partisan virtue

00:09:59.432 --> 00:10:01.734 align:start size:84% position:16%
signaling than in even
examining the data.

00:10:01.734 --> 00:10:03.703
That's the part that I
find really shocking.

00:10:03.703 --> 00:10:06.105 align:start size:97% position:3%
And the eagerness with which
people are going back to,

00:10:06.105 --> 00:10:07.607
"Well you're not masking."

00:10:07.607 --> 00:10:08.874 align:start size:97% position:3%
This is where it's gonna go,
right, they're gonna say,

00:10:08.874 --> 00:10:10.242
the CDC will issue some
sort of guidance saying

00:10:10.242 --> 00:10:11.811
if you're vaccinated,
you ought to mask up.

00:10:11.811 --> 00:10:12.712
And I'm going to say, no.

00:10:12.712 --> 00:10:14.246
I've already said no.

00:10:14.246 --> 00:10:16.616
I've vaccinated, I am not
transmitting the disease,

00:10:16.616 --> 00:10:18.951 line:0%
the numbers of people who are
asymptomatically transmitting

00:10:18.951 --> 00:10:20.820 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
COVID while vaccinated
is very low.

00:10:20.820 --> 00:10:22.855 line:0%
The number of breakthrough
infections is very, very low.

00:10:22.855 --> 00:10:24.890 line:0%
According to the New York Times
there are 160 million people

00:10:24.890 --> 00:10:26.459
vaccinated in the United States.

00:10:26.459 --> 00:10:28.461 align:start size:97% position:3%
There've been something like
6,000 breakthrough cases.

00:10:28.461 --> 00:10:29.929
I'm not masking up for that.

00:10:29.929 --> 00:10:31.397
And most of all, it's one
thing to make the case

00:10:31.397 --> 00:10:33.933 align:start size:97% position:3%
that I should mask up if
somebody can get the disease

00:10:33.933 --> 00:10:35.401
through no fault of their own.

00:10:35.401 --> 00:10:36.669 align:start size:97% position:3%
But if you've had the
opportunity to get a vaccine

00:10:36.669 --> 00:10:38.304
and then you didn't and
then I give you COVID,

00:10:38.304 --> 00:10:39.772
that one is kind of on you.

00:10:39.772 --> 00:10:41.240
That's really not on me anymore.

00:10:41.240 --> 00:10:43.309 align:start size:97% position:3%
But there will be this
move, like, if somebody says

00:10:43.309 --> 00:10:45.144
that you need to mask up
despite being vaccinated

00:10:45.144 --> 00:10:46.979
and you say no, then
it will be back to,

00:10:46.979 --> 00:10:48.514
"Oh, you're willing
to kill grandma."

00:10:48.514 --> 00:10:51.217
It's like, "No, I was never
willing to kill grandma."

00:10:51.217 --> 00:10:53.786 align:start size:88% position:13%
But it's become much
more about the partisan.

00:10:53.786 --> 00:10:55.221 align:start size:88% position:13%
It's why you see people
yelling at people

00:10:55.221 --> 00:10:56.789
who are un-vaccinated, right?

00:10:56.789 --> 00:10:58.791
It's not because they actually
want to convince those people

00:10:58.791 --> 00:11:00.626
to vaccinate, if you want to
convince somebody to vaccinate

00:11:00.626 --> 00:11:02.061 align:start size:88% position:13%
you do what I said
earlier, where you treat

00:11:02.061 --> 00:11:03.996 align:start size:97% position:3%
them as an individual human
being, you take a look

00:11:03.996 --> 00:11:05.431 align:start size:84% position:16%
at their risk factors,
you try to analyze

00:11:05.431 --> 00:11:07.733 align:start size:97% position:3%
those on an individual
level and assuage the fears.

00:11:07.733 --> 00:11:11.337
If you want to create
a sort of polarized,

00:11:11.337 --> 00:11:13.005 align:start size:88% position:13%
you're a bad person,
I'm a good person thing,

00:11:13.005 --> 00:11:14.674 align:start size:88% position:13%
then when you say you're
an idiot and a moron

00:11:14.674 --> 00:11:17.743
if you don't vaccinate on
my timeline as I see fit

00:11:17.743 --> 00:11:20.446 align:start size:84% position:16%
and no matter your
prior health scenario.

00:11:20.446 --> 00:11:23.549
- Right, you'll be proud
to know Ben, as a refugee

00:11:23.549 --> 00:11:26.519 align:start position:0%
of Los Angeles, that, you
know, we have this mask mandate

00:11:26.519 --> 00:11:27.653
in effect again.

00:11:27.653 --> 00:11:29.622 align:start size:88% position:13%
And I went to a
restaurant this weekend,

00:11:29.622 --> 00:11:32.391 align:start size:97% position:3%
I went to Home Depot this
weekend and I went to a mall

00:11:32.391 --> 00:11:34.827
this weekend and I
did not wear a mask.

00:11:34.827 --> 00:11:36.328
And guess what?

00:11:36.328 --> 00:11:38.464
An awful lot of people nodded
at me, you know, in support,

00:11:38.464 --> 00:11:40.733
a lot of people were
not wearing masks.

00:11:40.733 --> 00:11:42.334
And yes, when I went
into Bloomingdale's

00:11:42.334 --> 00:11:44.236
and they asked me to
put the mask on, I did

00:11:44.236 --> 00:11:46.338
because I'm not trying
to get somebody fired

00:11:46.338 --> 00:11:47.673 align:start size:84% position:16%
or get into a fight
with somebody.

00:11:47.673 --> 00:11:49.842 align:start size:84% position:16%
But I bring it up
because enough people

00:11:49.842 --> 00:11:53.479
are sort of like, "Okay,
it is time to move on."

00:11:53.479 --> 00:11:54.947
And that's just where
we're at at the moment.

00:11:54.947 --> 00:11:56.415
- Yeah.

00:11:56.415 --> 00:11:58.017 align:start position:0%
Well, again, I moved to Florida
and I will tell you this,

00:11:58.017 --> 00:12:00.019 align:start size:84% position:16%
if they try this
whole vaccinated need
to mask up again,

00:12:00.019 --> 00:12:01.487
nobody's doing it.

00:12:01.487 --> 00:12:02.922 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean people weren't
doing it originally here.

00:12:02.922 --> 00:12:05.091 align:start size:97% position:3%
I can't imagine that people
are gonna do it here.

00:12:05.091 --> 00:12:08.060
And again, you know, Governor
DeSantis has been very big

00:12:08.060 --> 00:12:09.462
on everybody should
get the vaccine,

00:12:09.462 --> 00:12:11.831 align:start size:88% position:13%
if you are physically
able to get the vaccine.

00:12:11.831 --> 00:12:14.200
And there's not much more
than that, that he can do.

00:12:14.200 --> 00:12:17.169 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I'm just, I gotta
say, just on a data level

00:12:17.169 --> 00:12:18.604
I'm bewildered by this.

00:12:18.604 --> 00:12:19.839 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was looking at the
seven day running average

00:12:19.839 --> 00:12:21.640
of death from COVID,
the average number

00:12:21.640 --> 00:12:23.342 align:start position:0%
of deaths from COVID, according
to the New York Times,

00:12:23.342 --> 00:12:25.945 align:start size:94% position:6%
seven day rolling
average right now is 269.

00:12:25.945 --> 00:12:27.446
Okay, when we were at the
height of the pandemic,

00:12:27.446 --> 00:12:29.615 align:start size:97% position:3%
it was well over 3,000
people a day who were dying.

00:12:29.615 --> 00:12:32.251
So we've brought down that
factor by a factor of 10.

00:12:32.251 --> 00:12:34.820 align:start size:94% position:6%
Okay, we are now seeing
fewer people die every day

00:12:34.820 --> 00:12:36.689
in the United States
from COVID than die

00:12:36.689 --> 00:12:38.924
on a normal day from diabetes.

00:12:38.924 --> 00:12:42.428 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Right, and 269, 269, I
mean, are they giving us ages

00:12:42.428 --> 00:12:44.663
on that or other health, you
know, the comorbidity stuff?

00:12:44.663 --> 00:12:46.432
Because that's a
very small number.

00:12:46.432 --> 00:12:48.467
Of course we don't
want people to die,

00:12:48.467 --> 00:12:49.735
but it's a small number.

00:12:49.735 --> 00:12:51.370
- Well, I mean, again,
if you are going to talk

00:12:51.370 --> 00:12:54.073 align:start position:0%
about public health crises
then you really do have to talk

00:12:54.073 --> 00:12:55.674
about the number of
people who are dying

00:12:55.674 --> 00:12:57.476
and the number of people
who are being hospitalized.

00:12:57.476 --> 00:12:59.245
And the fact that the media
will do things like play

00:12:59.245 --> 00:13:00.613
with stats where they'll say,
"Well, you know, we've had

00:13:00.613 --> 00:13:03.048
a 40% increase in the
number of hospitalized

00:13:03.048 --> 00:13:04.550
from three weeks ago."

00:13:04.550 --> 00:13:05.751
And it's like, "Yes, but
the number of hospitalized

00:13:05.751 --> 00:13:07.486
three weeks ago was
very, very low."

00:13:07.486 --> 00:13:10.489 align:start size:97% position:3%
Like a 40% increase means
we are still very, very low.

00:13:10.489 --> 00:13:11.991
So this doesn't mean
that we're making light

00:13:11.991 --> 00:13:13.459
of any of this sort of stuff.

00:13:13.459 --> 00:13:14.960
What it does mean is that
statistically speaking

00:13:14.960 --> 00:13:16.695 align:start position:0%
the people who are getting
serious breakthrough infections

00:13:16.695 --> 00:13:18.597 align:start size:84% position:16%
have significant
underlying illnesses,

00:13:18.597 --> 00:13:20.266 align:start size:84% position:16%
very significant
underlying illnesses,

00:13:20.266 --> 00:13:22.701 align:start size:97% position:3%
and the people who are
mostly getting hospitalized

00:13:22.701 --> 00:13:25.871
and the people who are
dying tend to be people

00:13:25.871 --> 00:13:27.406
who are un-vaccinated.

00:13:27.406 --> 00:13:29.775
And that really resides in
sort of the middle section

00:13:29.775 --> 00:13:31.177
of the age range
for the population

00:13:31.177 --> 00:13:33.445 align:start size:97% position:3%
because, dirty little
secret, pretty much everybody

00:13:33.445 --> 00:13:36.315
who's over the age of 65 in
this country got the vaccine.

00:13:36.315 --> 00:13:37.650
- Yeah.

00:13:37.650 --> 00:13:38.884 align:start size:97% position:3%
Ben, I'm not an
mathemagician like you are,

00:13:38.884 --> 00:13:40.319
but if there's one
person who had COVID

00:13:40.319 --> 00:13:41.720
and then the next
week there's two,

00:13:41.720 --> 00:13:43.856
what's the percent
increase on that?

00:13:43.856 --> 00:13:44.924
- That's a 100% increase.

00:13:44.924 --> 00:13:46.158
Right?

00:13:46.158 --> 00:13:47.526
- My God, that's a
huge, huge increase.

00:13:47.526 --> 00:13:49.662
All right, well all of
this leads us perfectly

00:13:49.662 --> 00:13:52.431 align:start size:97% position:3%
to "The Authoritarian
Moment" because it does seem

00:13:52.431 --> 00:13:55.634
like we are in it right now.

00:13:55.634 --> 00:13:57.736
Are you sort of having a pat
yourself on the back moment?

00:13:57.736 --> 00:13:59.371
'Cause I've been feeling
that a little bit lately.

00:13:59.371 --> 00:14:02.975
Like we were in a group of
people that were screaming

00:14:02.975 --> 00:14:06.011 align:start size:84% position:16%
about all of this
about five years ago.

00:14:06.011 --> 00:14:07.046
Not to say there weren't plenty

00:14:07.046 --> 00:14:08.581
of people doing it before that.

00:14:08.581 --> 00:14:11.350
But like we were really on
the internet like front end

00:14:11.350 --> 00:14:13.752 align:start size:88% position:13%
of like "Guys, this
horrible thing is here."

00:14:13.752 --> 00:14:14.954
And everyone kept saying,

00:14:14.954 --> 00:14:16.655
"No, no, it's just
on college campuses."

00:14:16.655 --> 00:14:19.758 align:start size:94% position:6%
And now it has burst
forth for everyone to see.

00:14:19.758 --> 00:14:21.260
- Yeah, no question.

00:14:21.260 --> 00:14:23.562
I mean, you know, I used to
think, as a religious Jew

00:14:23.562 --> 00:14:25.030
there's a whole
take on prophecy,

00:14:25.030 --> 00:14:27.366 align:start size:94% position:6%
that prophecy is like
God speaking through you,

00:14:27.366 --> 00:14:30.069 align:start size:97% position:3%
but I tend to think now
that prophecy is more along

00:14:30.069 --> 00:14:31.537
(indistinct) lines.

00:14:31.537 --> 00:14:34.273
Just seeing very clearly
what's happening right now.

00:14:34.273 --> 00:14:36.542
I mean, I think the reason
that that Orwell's "1984"

00:14:36.542 --> 00:14:38.177 align:start size:88% position:13%
is prophetic is not
because it was prophecy,

00:14:38.177 --> 00:14:39.712 align:start size:97% position:3%
it's because he was
actually describing a thing

00:14:39.712 --> 00:14:41.914
that was happening in the
Soviet Union at the time.

00:14:41.914 --> 00:14:43.716 align:start size:97% position:3%
And so when we look at
things happening elsewhere,

00:14:43.716 --> 00:14:45.217 align:start size:84% position:16%
like, "Wow, how
could he foresee it?"

00:14:45.217 --> 00:14:47.019
He wasn't foreseeing anything,
he was literally describing.

00:14:47.019 --> 00:14:50.322
And describing what's going
on, you know, five years ago

00:14:50.322 --> 00:14:51.590
and then looking
what's happening.

00:14:51.590 --> 00:14:52.825
It was a smaller
phenomenon then,

00:14:52.825 --> 00:14:54.393 align:start size:81% position:19%
it's a much larger
phenomenon now.

00:14:54.393 --> 00:14:55.895
And I don't think any
of us were prophets,

00:14:55.895 --> 00:14:58.297
I think that we just all saw
clearly what was happening

00:14:58.297 --> 00:14:59.732 align:start size:84% position:16%
and the direction that
people were moving.

00:14:59.732 --> 00:15:01.800 align:start size:97% position:3%
And the authoritarianism
that I talk about in the book

00:15:01.800 --> 00:15:05.070 align:start size:97% position:3%
is really not the government
top-down authoritarianism

00:15:05.070 --> 00:15:06.605
that we've worried
about in the past.

00:15:06.605 --> 00:15:08.073
The idea the government is
gonna tell you what to do,

00:15:08.073 --> 00:15:10.075
although that may be
the natural outgrowth

00:15:10.075 --> 00:15:13.245 align:start size:88% position:13%
of a sort of attitudinal
authoritarianism
that's taken over.

00:15:13.245 --> 00:15:15.648
What I'm talking about more
is all of the institutions

00:15:15.648 --> 00:15:17.716 align:start size:97% position:3%
of society, the
non-governmental institutions

00:15:17.716 --> 00:15:20.819
of society in large
