00:26:28.420 --> 00:26:30.255
So the Democrats are like,
"Well, you know, the lies

00:26:30.255 --> 00:26:32.924 align:start size:97% position:3%
about January 6th and November
4th, those are leading

00:26:32.924 --> 00:26:34.392
to all these voter fraud bills."

00:26:34.392 --> 00:26:36.227 align:start size:97% position:3%
Okay, even if that were
true the lies that you guys

00:26:36.227 --> 00:26:37.929 align:start size:84% position:16%
are telling about
voter suppression
have led to you trying

00:26:37.929 --> 00:26:39.598 align:start size:88% position:13%
to federalize the entire
system in violation

00:26:39.598 --> 00:26:40.865
of the constitution.

00:26:40.865 --> 00:26:42.801
You're right, the media
lie about this stuff

00:26:42.801 --> 00:26:45.303
on a routine basis and then
they obscure it by pretending

00:26:45.303 --> 00:26:46.771
that they're objective.

00:26:46.771 --> 00:26:49.274 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I think that their
day of dominance is ending

00:26:49.274 --> 00:26:51.843
which is why, I think that the
discussion over the fake news

00:26:51.843 --> 00:26:54.012
is actually secondary to the
discussion over social media,

00:26:54.012 --> 00:26:56.181
because what's happened
is that it used to be,

00:26:56.181 --> 00:26:57.882
they used to bookmark all
the sites that you wanted

00:26:57.882 --> 00:26:59.684
to visit, and this is the
old way of doing things

00:26:59.684 --> 00:27:01.152
in 2003, 2004, right.

00:27:01.152 --> 00:27:03.088 align:start size:97% position:3%
You'd bookmark Drudge and
then you'd bookmark, you know,

00:27:03.088 --> 00:27:04.856
the Huffington Post and
you'd actually check

00:27:04.856 --> 00:27:06.324
all the different
sites individually.

00:27:06.324 --> 00:27:07.959 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because everybody started
getting their news

00:27:07.959 --> 00:27:10.061 align:start size:97% position:3%
through these feeds, whether
it's Facebook or Twitter,

00:27:10.061 --> 00:27:12.197
the centralization
of news consumption,

00:27:12.197 --> 00:27:15.133
one source, has allowed
the left to swoop in

00:27:15.133 --> 00:27:17.402
and then try to bottleneck
the amount of information

00:27:17.402 --> 00:27:18.603
that can get out
via these sources.

00:27:18.603 --> 00:27:19.838 align:start size:84% position:16%
That's the part that's
really dangerous.

00:27:19.838 --> 00:27:20.772 align:start size:88% position:13%
I'm not worried about
the New York Times being

00:27:20.772 --> 00:27:22.240
a propaganda outfit.

00:27:22.240 --> 00:27:23.875 align:start position:0%
They've been a propaganda outfit
as long as I've been alive.

00:27:23.875 --> 00:27:26.778
I'm much more worried about
them trying to re-establish

00:27:26.778 --> 00:27:29.481
a monopolistic control
of the dissemination

00:27:29.481 --> 00:27:31.883 align:start size:97% position:3%
of information than I am
about them being who they are.

00:27:31.883 --> 00:27:33.752
- Yeah, so to that point,
can you talk a little bit

00:27:33.752 --> 00:27:36.388
about your position,
the difference between

00:27:36.388 --> 00:27:38.957 align:start size:88% position:13%
say a purely libertarian
position on big tech

00:27:38.957 --> 00:27:40.291
versus a conservative opinion?

00:27:40.291 --> 00:27:42.827 align:start size:88% position:13%
Because this is now
becoming the hot thing.

00:27:42.827 --> 00:27:44.396
It's like, maybe
there's no chance.

00:27:44.396 --> 00:27:46.164
Maybe this ship has sailed
and we can't do anything

00:27:46.164 --> 00:27:47.699
at this point.

00:27:47.699 --> 00:27:49.267
I'm guessing you don't want,
or at least I've never heard

00:27:49.267 --> 00:27:51.403
you say that you want, you
know, government regulators

00:27:51.403 --> 00:27:53.104 align:start size:94% position:6%
with hard hats, you
know, walking into Google

00:27:53.104 --> 00:27:54.539
to look at the algorithm.

00:27:54.539 --> 00:27:58.309 align:start position:0%
But what do you think we should
or could do, if anything?

00:27:58.309 --> 00:28:00.845 align:start size:94% position:6%
- So I think that the
pretty easy solution here

00:28:00.845 --> 00:28:04.616 align:start size:97% position:3%
seems to be to make a minor
change to section 230.

00:28:04.616 --> 00:28:06.184 align:start size:88% position:13%
And the minor change
would be to just get rid

00:28:06.184 --> 00:28:07.652
of the catch all clause.

00:28:07.652 --> 00:28:10.121
So if you'd take a look at
section 230, section 230 says

00:28:10.121 --> 00:28:13.725
that we, that you are
relieved from liability

00:28:13.725 --> 00:28:16.761
if you remove, for example,
obscenity or pornography

00:28:16.761 --> 00:28:19.531 align:start position:0%
or violent material or anything
otherwise objectionable.

00:28:19.531 --> 00:28:21.399 align:start size:88% position:13%
It's that anything
otherwise objectionable

00:28:21.399 --> 00:28:23.835
that is the catchall provision.

00:28:23.835 --> 00:28:26.104
And I understand why
this originally was.

00:28:26.104 --> 00:28:28.673 align:start position:0%
Right, to understand why section
230 is drawn the way it is

00:28:28.673 --> 00:28:29.974
you have to understand
the history a little bit.

00:28:29.974 --> 00:28:31.643 align:start size:84% position:16%
Basically platforms
were created,

00:28:31.643 --> 00:28:33.178 align:start size:84% position:16%
these platforms
were open platforms,

00:28:33.178 --> 00:28:35.613
and then there was, and
you didn't have liability

00:28:35.613 --> 00:28:37.549
for what was on the platform
so long as you didn't police

00:28:37.549 --> 00:28:38.783
what was on the platform

00:28:38.783 --> 00:28:39.718
because it was just
like a phone line.

00:28:39.718 --> 00:28:41.152
Right?

00:28:41.152 --> 00:28:42.387 align:start size:97% position:3%
What I say on the phone
line, if I threaten to murder

00:28:42.387 --> 00:28:43.354
somebody, AT&amp;T's not
responsible for that.

00:28:43.354 --> 00:28:45.056
I'm responsible for that.

00:28:45.056 --> 00:28:47.092
Okay, so platforms
were basically just
you post something,

00:28:47.092 --> 00:28:49.828
the platform is not responsible
for the thing that you post.

00:28:49.828 --> 00:28:52.163 align:start size:88% position:13%
Then there was a website
that started going in

00:28:52.163 --> 00:28:53.598 align:start size:84% position:16%
and deleting all the
obscene material.

00:28:53.598 --> 00:28:56.067 align:start position:0%
And the people who were
putting up the obscene material

00:28:56.067 --> 00:29:00.105 align:start position:0%
they said, "You've now violated,
you're now a publisher.

00:29:00.105 --> 00:29:02.574 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because you're editing
and you're deleting stuff,

00:29:02.574 --> 00:29:03.775
this makes you a publisher.

00:29:03.775 --> 00:29:05.143
So if somebody posts
something to defamatory

00:29:05.143 --> 00:29:07.011
and you don't delete
it, you're a publisher,

00:29:07.011 --> 00:29:08.947 align:start size:88% position:13%
you ought to be treated
with liability."

00:29:08.947 --> 00:29:10.582
And so Congress said,
"Well, that seems weird

00:29:10.582 --> 00:29:13.351
that if I decide to get rid
of obscenity it's now my job

00:29:13.351 --> 00:29:16.421 align:start size:94% position:6%
to treat the entire
platform as a publisher."

00:29:16.421 --> 00:29:18.523
Well the problem is that has
now been completely reversed.

00:29:18.523 --> 00:29:21.526
The idea behind 230 was to
promulgate and allow people

00:29:21.526 --> 00:29:23.828 align:start size:84% position:16%
to get rid of truly
objectionable material

00:29:23.828 --> 00:29:25.597 align:start size:84% position:16%
while not absorbing
the liability

00:29:25.597 --> 00:29:27.565
of becoming like the Daily
Wire or the New York Times,

00:29:27.565 --> 00:29:28.933
having to fact check every post,

00:29:28.933 --> 00:29:30.468
because it's an open platform.

00:29:30.468 --> 00:29:32.537
Instead what the left did is
they reversed the polarity.

00:29:32.537 --> 00:29:34.873
They said, "Well actually
the job now of section 230

00:29:34.873 --> 00:29:36.975 align:start size:81% position:19%
is to make you
into a publisher."

00:29:36.975 --> 00:29:38.510
Right?

00:29:38.510 --> 00:29:39.978
"Now your job is to remove all
of the objectionable content,

00:29:39.978 --> 00:29:42.013
including politically
objectionable content.

00:29:42.013 --> 00:29:43.915
And we will threaten
you with getting rid

00:29:43.915 --> 00:29:47.152 align:start size:97% position:3%
of all section 230 protections
if you don't get rid

00:29:47.152 --> 00:29:48.787
of," quote unquote,
"misinformation."

00:29:48.787 --> 00:29:51.489
Well the easy way to fix
this is to just get rid

00:29:51.489 --> 00:29:53.024 align:start size:84% position:16%
of the otherwise
objectionable clause.

00:29:53.024 --> 00:29:55.794
Meaning that you can get rid
of stuff that violates the law.

00:29:55.794 --> 00:29:57.996 align:start size:88% position:13%
You can get rid of stuff
that is pornographic.

00:29:57.996 --> 00:30:00.832 align:start size:97% position:3%
You can get rid of
repeated spam, for example.

00:30:00.832 --> 00:30:02.534 align:start size:97% position:3%
But if you start
discriminating on the basis

00:30:02.534 --> 00:30:04.869 align:start size:84% position:16%
of politics, you're
no longer a publisher,

00:30:04.869 --> 00:30:06.938 align:start size:97% position:3%
you're no longer a platform,
now you're a publisher

00:30:06.938 --> 00:30:08.606
and the liability attaches.

00:30:08.606 --> 00:30:10.842
- But do you think we have a
government or any officials?

00:30:10.842 --> 00:30:13.144 align:start position:0%
I mean, there's a couple of
Republicans talking about this,

00:30:13.144 --> 00:30:15.380
you know, Mike Lee and
Jim Jordan, Ryan Paul.

00:30:15.380 --> 00:30:16.881
I mean a few people.

00:30:16.881 --> 00:30:18.983
But it's like, do you think
we have any political will

00:30:18.983 --> 00:30:21.486 align:start size:97% position:3%
to actually ever do anything
other than have hearings

00:30:21.486 --> 00:30:22.720
about this stuff?

00:30:22.720 --> 00:30:24.222
Like you think they
can do something?

00:30:24.222 --> 00:30:25.423
- Well the problem is that
everybody says they want

00:30:25.423 --> 00:30:26.224 align:start size:88% position:13%
to do something but
the stuff they wanna do

00:30:26.224 --> 00:30:27.425 line:0%
is radically different.

00:30:27.425 --> 00:30:28.760 line:0%
So Democrats are not
in favor of getting rid

00:30:28.760 --> 00:30:30.395 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
of the otherwise
objectionable clause

00:30:30.395 --> 00:30:32.163 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
because that would do
what we're talking about,

00:30:32.163 --> 00:30:33.865 line:0%
it would open up the platforms.

00:30:33.865 --> 00:30:35.633
Instead what they
would like to do

00:30:35.633 --> 00:30:37.202
is close off the platform.

00:30:37.202 --> 00:30:39.804
So what they would like to do
is treat Facebook as monopoly

00:30:39.804 --> 00:30:41.873
and then have somebody sit
on top of the government,

00:30:41.873 --> 00:30:44.409 align:start size:84% position:16%
like an Elizabeth
Warren appointee, and
decide what Facebook

00:30:44.409 --> 00:30:45.710
can and cannot put up.

00:30:45.710 --> 00:30:47.212
And that of course is
incredibly dangerous.

00:30:47.212 --> 00:30:49.147
So you'll see these New York
Times articles where it's like,

00:30:49.147 --> 00:30:50.682
"Ah, there's broad
spectrum agreement

00:30:50.682 --> 00:30:52.250
that Facebook has
to be regulated."

00:30:52.250 --> 00:30:54.986
Well, I mean, that's
really not correct.

00:30:54.986 --> 00:30:56.821
I mean, the question
is what is the content

00:30:56.821 --> 00:30:58.389
of the regulation?

00:30:58.389 --> 00:31:01.159 align:start size:97% position:3%
It's like saying that my
child and I have an agreement

00:31:01.159 --> 00:31:02.961
that there ought
to be consequences

00:31:02.961 --> 00:31:04.395
for not doing your homework.

00:31:04.395 --> 00:31:05.897 align:start size:97% position:3%
Yeah, my child's consequence
is that she would like

00:31:05.897 --> 00:31:07.098
to be able to eat cookies.

00:31:07.098 --> 00:31:08.600 align:start size:84% position:16%
My consequence is
she goes to her room.

00:31:08.600 --> 00:31:09.901
Like we agree that there
ought to be consequences,

00:31:09.901 --> 00:31:11.903
but these are wildly variant.

00:31:11.903 --> 00:31:13.404
- Yeah, all right.

00:31:13.404 --> 00:31:14.906 align:start size:97% position:3%
So let's just jump into each
chapter for a little bit.

00:31:14.906 --> 00:31:17.475
We've sort of bounced around
through some of them already.

00:31:17.475 --> 00:31:20.245 align:start size:94% position:6%
"How to Silence a
Majority," is chapter one

00:31:20.245 --> 00:31:24.749
and it does feel like most
people have been silenced

00:31:24.749 --> 00:31:28.319 align:start size:97% position:3%
just by their own
acquiescence to all of this.

00:31:28.319 --> 00:31:29.954
- Yeah, that's right.

00:31:29.954 --> 00:31:32.957 align:start size:84% position:16%
Basically all it takes
to silence a majority
is a very loud,

00:31:32.957 --> 00:31:34.759 align:start size:84% position:16%
very aggressive and
intransigent minority.

00:31:34.759 --> 00:31:37.729 align:start size:97% position:3%
You can re-normalize an
entire institution by using,

00:31:37.729 --> 00:31:40.031 align:start size:97% position:3%
by getting maybe 20% of
people inside an institution

00:31:40.031 --> 00:31:42.300 align:start size:84% position:16%
to be very loud
and very solidified

00:31:42.300 --> 00:31:44.702 align:start size:97% position:3%
and repeating the same thing
over and over and over.

00:31:44.702 --> 00:31:46.471
Which of course is what
the left is very good at.

00:31:46.471 --> 00:31:47.972 align:start size:88% position:13%
And you can see this
happen in your own life.

00:31:47.972 --> 00:31:50.208 align:start size:97% position:3%
Like the example that's used
by Nassim Nicholas Taleb

00:31:50.208 --> 00:31:54.145
is the example of you have a
family of four and the daughter

00:31:54.145 --> 00:31:55.647
decides one day
she's vegetarian.

00:31:55.647 --> 00:31:58.283 align:start size:97% position:3%
So she comes home, she says
to mom, "I'm vegetarian

00:31:58.283 --> 00:31:59.918
and I want a vegetarian meal."

00:31:59.918 --> 00:32:01.853
And mom says, "Okay, well I
can either make two meals,

00:32:01.853 --> 00:32:03.121
one that's vegetarian for her

00:32:03.121 --> 00:32:04.656
and one that's good
for everybody else,

00:32:04.656 --> 00:32:06.991 align:start size:94% position:6%
or I can make a vegetarian
meal for everyone."

00:32:06.991 --> 00:32:08.026
And so mom decides I'm making

00:32:08.026 --> 00:32:09.494
a vegetarian meal for everyone.

00:32:09.494 --> 00:32:11.229
Well, daughter has now
re-normalized the family.

00:32:11.229 --> 00:32:12.463
The family's now vegetarian

00:32:12.463 --> 00:32:13.731
because daughter
was intransigent.

00:32:13.731 --> 00:32:15.233
And you can expand
that outward, right?

00:32:15.233 --> 00:32:16.734 align:start size:94% position:6%
The whole family now wants
to go to a block party,

00:32:16.734 --> 00:32:18.202 align:start size:84% position:16%
they say to the person
at the block party,

00:32:18.202 --> 00:32:20.305 align:start size:97% position:3%
"We need a vegetarian meal
for us, because our daughter."

00:32:20.305 --> 00:32:22.273 align:start size:97% position:3%
And the person says, "Okay,
do I really want to, you know,

00:32:22.273 --> 00:32:23.107
go out and buy two meals.

00:32:23.107 --> 00:32:24.642
I'll buy one meal."

00:32:24.642 --> 00:32:25.910
Now everybody's vegetarian
'cause of this one person.

00:32:25.910 --> 00:32:27.178
You can see that sort
of stuff happening

00:32:27.178 --> 00:32:28.713
inside our institutions.

00:32:28.713 --> 00:32:30.715
It requires intransigence,
and it requires solidity.

00:32:30.715 --> 00:32:32.016
You can't move on the position,

00:32:32.016 --> 00:32:33.518 align:start size:84% position:16%
you have to be
really intransigent

00:32:33.518 --> 00:32:35.720
and the imposition that
you're making on somebody

00:32:35.720 --> 00:32:37.388
has to be just minor enough

00:32:37.388 --> 00:32:39.023
that they don't really
fight back against you.

00:32:39.023 --> 00:32:40.692 align:start size:97% position:3%
Right, it can't be something
where you like demand

00:32:40.692 --> 00:32:42.560
that you're gonna be the,
that you are the captain,

00:32:42.560 --> 00:32:44.062
like you run the place now.

00:32:44.062 --> 00:32:45.897
It can't be that, it has to
be something where, you know,

00:32:45.897 --> 00:32:47.432
we just want diversity training.

00:32:47.432 --> 00:32:48.433
That's all we want.

00:32:48.433 --> 00:32:49.901
We just want diversity training.

00:32:49.901 --> 00:32:51.569 align:start size:97% position:3%
And if we get diversity
training, then we'll be happy

00:32:51.569 --> 00:32:53.604
and we'll leave you alone
and won't go go make our HR

00:32:53.604 --> 00:32:56.207
reports and won't file lawsuits
and everything will be good.

00:32:56.207 --> 00:32:57.976
And people in the middle
are like, "Well, you know,

00:32:57.976 --> 00:32:59.711
it's annoying but do
I really want to spend

00:32:59.711 --> 00:33:00.945
my day doing this?"

00:33:00.945 --> 00:33:03.781
And soon it escalates
from, "Okay, we need

00:33:05.216 --> 00:33:07.919 align:start size:97% position:3%
this anti-discrimination,
we need diversity training,"

00:33:07.919 --> 00:33:10.388 align:start size:84% position:16%
to, "We need active
anti-racism training."

00:33:10.388 --> 00:33:11.622
And now you got Deborah
Max Kennedy in there.

00:33:11.622 --> 00:33:13.157 align:start size:88% position:13%
And they figure, "Okay,
well, 10,000 bucks,

00:33:13.157 --> 00:33:14.692 align:start size:84% position:16%
we can get these
people off our back."

00:33:14.692 --> 00:33:16.294
Deborah Max Kennedy comes
in, spouts some bull crap

00:33:16.294 --> 00:33:17.929 align:start size:81% position:19%
and we all move
on with our lives.

00:33:17.929 --> 00:33:19.430 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they say, "Well, yeah,
but here's the thing,

00:33:19.430 --> 00:33:20.698
you haven't established
the principles of equity.

00:33:20.698 --> 00:33:23.101
We need hiring based on race."

00:33:23.101 --> 00:33:25.203 align:start size:94% position:6%
And now you start saying,
"Okay, well, I don't

00:33:25.203 --> 00:33:27.872
really like that but I'm also
afraid that if I fight back

00:33:27.872 --> 00:33:30.041
against you, you might
file some sort of lawsuit

00:33:30.041 --> 00:33:32.010 align:start size:94% position:6%
and claim that I'm
discriminating against you

00:33:32.010 --> 00:33:33.211
and you might lead a walkout.

00:33:33.211 --> 00:33:35.113 align:start size:88% position:13%
So I guess we'll go
along with that maybe."

00:33:35.113 --> 00:33:37.382
And then it's everybody at
the company needs to put

00:33:37.382 --> 00:33:38.616
out a black square.

00:33:38.616 --> 00:33:40.118
Right, you can see how
it just moves along.

00:33:40.118 --> 00:33:42.220
Because the more you give, the
more you're willing to give.

00:33:42.220 --> 00:33:43.921
- Does that also tell
you a little something

00:33:43.921 --> 00:33:45.356
about the human condition.

00:33:45.356 --> 00:33:46.824 align:start size:94% position:6%
'Cause as you were talking
about that, I mean,

00:33:46.824 --> 00:33:48.559 align:start size:97% position:3%
you could have given the exact
same examples with COVID.

00:33:48.559 --> 00:33:49.961
It was two weeks to
flatten the curve.

00:33:49.961 --> 00:33:51.429
It was, you know, a
month of lockdown.

00:33:51.429 --> 00:33:52.597
Now it's a year
and a half later,

00:33:52.597 --> 00:33:54.032
let's mask vaccinated people.

00:33:54.032 --> 00:33:55.633 align:start size:84% position:16%
I mean, it's just
something about humans

00:33:55.633 --> 00:33:58.403
and how much we just give
in the face of tyranny.

00:33:58.403 --> 00:33:59.937
Right?

00:33:59.937 --> 00:34:01.172
- I mean one of the great
lies about human beings

00:34:01.172 --> 00:34:01.839
is that we're very
confrontational.

00:34:01.839 --> 00:34:02.774
We are not.

00:34:02.774 --> 00:34:04.275
We are very conflict averse.

00:34:04.275 --> 00:34:07.278 align:start size:97% position:3%
And people who are conflict
seeking tend to be the winners

00:34:07.278 --> 00:34:09.914
in this particular game
theory situation, right?

00:34:09.914 --> 00:34:11.949 align:start size:97% position:3%
It's like the kid in high
school who's the craziest kid

00:34:11.949 --> 00:34:13.217
no one wanted to fight.

00:34:13.217 --> 00:34:14.752
And maybe you could
beat him in a fight,

00:34:14.752 --> 00:34:16.254
