00:37:20.071 --> 00:37:22.673
So in some ways it's like,
yeah, they did all want this

00:37:22.673 --> 00:37:26.277
because now federal bailouts,
suddenly California has money,

00:37:26.277 --> 00:37:28.579
even though money
isn't worth much.

00:37:28.579 --> 00:37:29.814
Inflation?

00:37:29.814 --> 00:37:30.881 align:start size:81% position:19%
That's not a thing
anymore, right?

00:37:30.881 --> 00:37:32.383
- Yeah.

00:37:32.383 --> 00:37:33.851
I mean the basic idea from
the left has always been

00:37:33.851 --> 00:37:35.686 align:start size:97% position:3%
that emergency is a ratchet,
it's a one-way ratchet.

00:37:35.686 --> 00:37:37.488
And whether you're talking
about the Great Depression

00:37:37.488 --> 00:37:39.123 align:start size:84% position:16%
or World War II, or
whether you're talking

00:37:39.123 --> 00:37:41.959 align:start size:84% position:16%
about the so-called
war on poverty,

00:37:41.959 --> 00:37:44.495
and certainly now every
crisis is an opportunity

00:37:44.495 --> 00:37:45.696
to grow government.

00:37:45.696 --> 00:37:47.632 align:start size:88% position:13%
And because the left
thinks not only in terms

00:37:47.632 --> 00:37:50.001 align:start size:97% position:3%
of institutional control but
in terms of doing things,

00:37:50.001 --> 00:37:51.636
right, the way that you
